WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:43.200
Lightweight Vaseline
from the tour leader?

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.566
(Buying snacks at the dollar store)

00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:53.066
The server kept explaining
how to eat the skewers.

00:00:56.366 --> 00:00:57.833
This is a cucumber salad.

00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:00.466
I finally made it from the countryside to the
city (I was at Lake Kawaguchi a few days ago).

00:01:00.566 --> 00:01:01.533
You can really experience
Japan. I'm Hiker CP,

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.966
and right now I'm at a

00:01:18.366 --> 00:01:20.100
Location of Kamikochi. As for
the route to Kamikochi,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.666
I'm heading to Japan this time.

00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:23.966
Climbing my first mountain in Japan—or
maybe it was my second,

00:01:25.466 --> 00:01:28.266
since a few days ago I was at

00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:31.433
I was thinking we could try a day

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:32.233
hike up Mount Fuji—a quick hike.

00:01:32.233 --> 00:01:33.900
But it wasn't meant to be—because
of the typhoon,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.366
so now we're heading
to the second one.

00:01:37.366 --> 00:01:39.366
Hyōginza—but it’s kind of a bummer
because of the Mount Tsubakuro route

00:01:39.366 --> 00:01:41.000
The Zhongfang Hot Springs connection has
been cut off. It used to be "A in,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.700
B out," but now it's "B in, B out."

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.800
That's Shanggao Di. We were originally
supposed to come down this way.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.533
We're going to take this route
up to the highlands—going

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.100
up and down the same path.

00:01:51.966 --> 00:01:53.166
Our guide this

00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:55.400
time: Bo Ka

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.666
Yesterday I stayed in a part of Matsumoto
that was quite similar to Taiwan.

00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:00.466
Puli (??—that's just where
it's used as a...)

00:02:00.466 --> 00:02:03.066
From the meeting point to the
various hiking trails—this

00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:05.933
is a very popular route
in Japan called

00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:09.100
Although I do find this
name a little puzzling

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.866
Why were the Northern Alps named

00:02:11.866 --> 00:02:13.200
after the European Alps?

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.700
I'll take a closer look at
this when I get there.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.900
I'm really a newbie—I don't
know this route at all.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:18.900
Pacing, distance, elevation gain.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.900
.. but I didn't do my
homework either XDDD

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.500
Since this was a group tour (sigh... but the pre
-trip briefing was very thorough)

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.000
Because when you go hiking in Japan,
mountain huts are very convenient—I don't know.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.700
Just how convenient is it? I don't
think it's challenging enough—if

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.066
it's not challenging enough,
I suddenly won't be able to hike anymore.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.400
I still brought quite a lot of food,
and then...

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.966
You're not allowed to bring cooking stoves—but actually,
you can. Apparently...

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:35.466
Mountain House can be cooked.  People have been
trying to talk me out of it the whole time.

00:02:35.533 --> 00:02:36.433
But I still couldn't resist bringing

00:02:36.433 --> 00:02:38.866
a bowl and a titanium cup this time.

00:02:38.866 --> 00:02:41.100
Let me tell you all about the
culture shock I experienced

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.100
while hiking in Japan—just
how shocking it really was.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:43.900
Hey, guys! This is where the bus
stops and the visitor center

00:02:45.633 --> 00:02:49.000
(the drop
-off point for the Shanggao-Xiaji route).

00:02:49.233 --> 00:02:50.000
So all the visitors gather here

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.866
to climb different routes.

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.666
You can drink it straight.  I found out later
that the water in Japan is safe to drink.

00:02:54.666 --> 00:02:58.033
You can drink the water from the room,
but I still boil it first.

00:02:58.066 --> 00:02:59.066
I brought a water filter this time,

00:02:59.066 --> 00:03:00.933
so there's no need to worry too much.

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:02.700
So many Japanese girls &gt;//&lt; Let's

00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:06.133
head to Kappa Bridge first

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.666
There were really a lot of people.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.700
Kappa Bridge is very
rustic—and clean.

00:03:26.733 --> 00:03:28.033
Try a sip of this water—it tastes

00:03:30.833 --> 00:03:31.666
better than the water in the room.

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:34.533
It really does make a difference.
I'm still used to drinking water from the wilderness.

00:03:34.566 --> 00:03:35.466
I use plain water to

00:03:35.466 --> 00:03:36.800
chill this drink.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.833
They're releasing these super cute 110
-gram items

00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:42.500
in all sorts of designs
because of the bear.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.200
Xiong Xiong, are there just too many
Xiong Xiong in Japan??  So I believe

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.833
A lot of people have already heard
a whole bunch of noises just now.

00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:48.333
Wearing this bear bell—personally,

00:03:50.066 --> 00:03:51.500
I think it'll just attract
more of them XD

00:03:56.433 --> 00:03:57.800
I've heard this is a
famous bird in Japan.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.033
I hope I get to see it this time.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.766
I suppose every prefecture
has its own sake,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.300
and some come from Yamanashi
Prefecture.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.633
Mount Fuji, Yamanashi Prefecture,

00:04:07.633 --> 00:04:09.533
Matsumoto??

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:12.333
Which prefecture is Matsumoto in?
Shinshu? That’s why there

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:15.533
are so many Shinshu sakes—one
from every prefecture.

00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:16.233
A huge amount of alcohol;

00:04:20.366 --> 00:04:21.100
most of the tourists

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.233
If you come this far,

00:04:24.233 --> 00:04:26.166
just head back—just a quick stroll. If you really want to go hiking,
head that way—and this way.

00:04:26.166 --> 00:04:29.300
It was the Suiko Traverse, and then we hiked the Omote
-Ginza-Yari-dake route.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.200
It includes the Three Mountains
of Baima—this is one of them.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.833
I see it says "Central Tateyama."

00:04:32.833 --> 00:04:34.166
If you want to hike 100K on this

00:04:34.166 --> 00:04:36.500
route in the Northern Alps

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.833
I believe there will be no problem,

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:39.033
Azusagawa.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:42.100
Should I be? My Chinese is really bad XD (Self
-introduction

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.066
time! 19 people in total)

00:04:48.866 --> 00:04:50.566
First, walk a 3km trail.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:09.866
When you reach the first thing in Suigao,
there's something there.

00:05:09.866 --> 00:05:11.866
I think it's better to keep
walking along this path.

00:05:11.866 --> 00:05:15.133
The supply trucks only come at night,
otherwise...

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.200
The supplies at the mountain
lodge (I don't know

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.200
how to get them) include
set meals and alcohol.

00:05:19.533 --> 00:05:23.633
You can grab a meal here; the Kappa
Bridge leads to this side.

00:05:23.633 --> 00:05:26.633
Following this route,

00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:28.266
I'll ascend to Yamagata (I'm so hungry,
I need to eat one too XD).

00:05:29.266 --> 00:05:30.766
We are now tracing the stream,

00:05:30.766 --> 00:05:32.900
Wanda Nanxi.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.866
It's very chill to get to this
spot by following the stream.

00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:37.733
We'll be there soon.

00:05:37.733 --> 00:05:39.400
Dinner (slip of the tongue)
Lunch is coming up soon.

00:05:43.866 --> 00:05:45.566
He was so startled that he started stuttering when it
was time to eat after walking only a short distance.

00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:50.833
The alcohol is accompanied by a

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:53.300
bunch of super cute TNF socks.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.200
(It's actually really cheap)

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.100
Curry noodles + extra white rice

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:03.433
(Delicious but a bit salty)

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:29.300
(Super cute for kids)

00:06:31.933 --> 00:06:34.966
Once you arrive at Yokoo,

00:06:34.966 --> 00:06:37.366
you'll find it's a place for after
-school tutoring, with many after-school teachers here.

00:06:37.366 --> 00:06:42.033
There's a lot of room for learning,
with students bringing teachers along (?).

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:46.400
The teacher took the students to a campsite,
but it's uncertain.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:51.866
Why is there another option for keeping it open
for a long time? I think it's quite...

00:06:51.866 --> 00:06:55.300
The cool thing is that you can
check the weather in real time.

00:06:56.533 --> 00:06:59.766
The place we're going to is located
at the location of Yamagata.

00:06:59.766 --> 00:07:02.566
Are we staying at the Gunze
Villa today? Is it true that

00:07:03.433 --> 00:07:09.500
we have to enter the Gunze
Mountain Villa at 3 PM?

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.666
Gun
-dake? Anyway,

00:07:16.866 --> 00:07:25.633
it's going to rain before dinner. A 67
-gram umbrella, just the right size for first-time use.

00:07:25.633 --> 00:07:28.533
Use this 5
-ribbed umbrella when walking on a windless

00:07:28.533 --> 00:07:34.266
and fairly wide road (it's
super lightweight!).

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:55.000
At 4 o'clock sharp,

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.866
the guide led five and a half people up 5100km (15km).
Today was a very easy day.

00:07:59.866 --> 00:08:01.966
The route involved walking at a mid
-altitude

00:08:01.966 --> 00:08:03.166
location and then eating
a very filling meal.

00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:03.766
I'm dizzy from eating charcoal XD

00:08:03.766 --> 00:08:05.833
I'm going to eat it again later

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.066
Anyway, this is roughly the tempo
for mountain climbing in Japan.

00:08:09.633 --> 00:08:14.033
So don't worry about not having enough to eat,
I'll get you more rice later!

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:17.433
As for rations,

00:08:17.433 --> 00:08:21.500
I think a moderate amount is fine; I really
don't need bread to make you feel full.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.033
I still have two loaves of bread in my backpack,
so I need to think...

00:08:24.033 --> 00:08:26.900
The solution is to eat it tomorrow.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.166
It's said that it's easy to encounter
it in the afternoon in August.

00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:31.666
This kind of weather would be better
in September or October,

00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:35.833
since it's a high
-latitude country after all.

00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:44.800
The pillows and comforters are very comfortable,
so there's no need to bring your own pillow.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.600
It's not very thick; if it gets cold,
just bring your own warm clothes.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:53.533
He said that you need a
separate unit to cook

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:57.533
your own food if you
live outside, so...

00:08:57.533 --> 00:09:00.533
A top
-loading furnace won't work; what's the logic behind

00:09:00.533 --> 00:09:04.966
that? Does that mean we can't
eat five light meals?

00:09:04.966 --> 00:09:06.900
Everyone is brushing their teeth now.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.633
Japanese people brush their teeth at a very consistent
time; everyone is brushing their teeth.

00:09:12.766 --> 00:09:14.133
The talk room is really cool,

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:21.433
and you can read comics here.

00:09:21.433 --> 00:09:27.033
The room has tons of comics
and all sorts of shoes,

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:31.933
all neatly arranged.

00:09:31.933 --> 00:09:32.833
Bunk beds are

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.466
super hot

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:46.433
What can I soak in while soaking in a
hot spring (hot water is provided)?

00:09:46.433 --> 00:09:50.400
The food is still being prepared
in the charging area.

00:09:50.533 --> 00:09:55.233
Because I've grown my hair long now,
it's not the lightweight comb from the restaurant.

00:09:55.233 --> 00:10:00.200
I've finished showering,

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.633
so I can use the comb to comb my hair. If you come to Japan and encounter a hot spring while hiking,
you definitely should!

00:10:03.633 --> 00:10:07.800
Go take a shower! (Highly recommended!) Just scoop out
the hot water from the two bathtubs and turn it on.

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:11.166
Take a cold shower,

00:10:11.166 --> 00:10:12.733
sit there in the Japanese
public bathhouse.

00:10:12.733 --> 00:10:14.000
Your... penis and testicles

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.600
(??) will hang on the bench.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.200
After showering,

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.533
you can go down to soak in the
stainless steel hot spring.

00:10:20.533 --> 00:10:21.833
A tub with two stainless steel

00:10:21.833 --> 00:10:23.033
sections can hold three men.

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:25.700
Too tight (that area
is too big) Only two

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.600
There is water here,

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:29.700
but I don't know where
the hot water comes from.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:30.600
It's so clean now,

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.033
it feels amazing! Don't even think about
how many there were in front of you.

00:10:33.033 --> 00:10:36.166
Boys, go down to wash and don't
think about this.

00:10:36.166 --> 00:10:40.133
It feels great and it's
very clean.

00:10:40.133 --> 00:10:42.133
I only wear the same pair of underwear
and then change into clean ones.

00:10:42.133 --> 00:10:47.500
I just threw in my daily t
-shirt (STATIC) and fox-print shorts.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.966
Go to the drying room and you'll
find towels; just

00:10:49.966 --> 00:10:53.600
stand near the air vent and
they'll dry quickly.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:55.533
Because it's super hot there and
we have to wait until 6 PM for lunch,

00:10:55.533 --> 00:10:57.366
we're just lazing around for now.

00:10:57.866 --> 00:10:59.166
Keep combing my

00:10:59.166 --> 00:11:00.533
hair! Doggy!

00:11:01.833 --> 00:11:04.166
Dinner was at six o'clock

00:11:04.166 --> 00:11:08.166
(a super lavish meal!).

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:15.700
Fried chicken, fish,
and vegetables should make a mini canelé.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.166
(Super hot rice is so satisfying!)
(You can even

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:20.966
get more miso soup after
you finish it.)

00:11:25.733 --> 00:11:28.100
I've made beer!! I'm going
to make whey tea (too hot),

00:11:39.033 --> 00:11:43.000
so I'll add some cold water.

00:11:44.633 --> 00:11:48.900
It's almost 8 o'clock,

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.533
time to brush my teeth.
Tomorrow I need to get up at 5 and leave at 6.

00:11:52.533 --> 00:11:56.133
6K steep climb up 1200
meters. Anyway,

00:11:56.133 --> 00:11:58.400
we didn't climb
any mountains today.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.133
Taking a walk is normal; we're

00:11:59.133 --> 00:12:00.700
going to climb tomorrow.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:02.500
The mountain is 3100 meters high,

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.566
so we'll start at an altitude of 1800 meters. That's right,
we need to climb 1300 meters.

00:12:04.566 --> 00:12:08.700
Tomorrow will be tough,

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.300
anyway, I ate too much again,
ate too much at night, and ate two meals.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.866
I ate too much rice XD,
then ate canelé.

00:12:12.866 --> 00:12:16.733
These calories will come
in handy tomorrow.

00:12:16.866 --> 00:12:18.866
Although I'll be adding just as
much stuff again tomorrow (lol,

00:12:19.233 --> 00:12:22.800
haha), this is mountain
climbing in Japan.

00:12:23.933 --> 00:12:25.000
Special

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.033
OK

00:12:26.033 --> 00:12:28.366
Let's go to sleep,

00:12:37.166 --> 00:12:41.366
doggy! All the capsules we brought
this time—taurine, RC...

00:12:41.366 --> 00:12:45.966
Focus (taurine, repair (RC) to restore fatigue,
green tea caffeine)

00:12:45.966 --> 00:12:50.300
Electrolysis, replenishing electrolytes
and boosting immunity

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:55.266
O2 capsules can increase
oxygen levels,

00:12:55.266 --> 00:12:57.933
which is helpful at high altitudes, as can Zone4 acid
-resistant capsules.

00:12:57.933 --> 00:13:00.066
Now I eat very little here,

00:13:00.066 --> 00:13:02.866
mainly because of the electrolytic
activity...

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:05.300
Japanese people eat very salty food,

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.333
so they need to eat several bowls of miso
soup to replenish their salt intake.

00:13:08.333 --> 00:13:10.433
You can charge it back,
but you can still recharge it on the way.

00:13:10.433 --> 00:13:12.266
Two because there was not much
food to eat on the way.

00:13:12.266 --> 00:13:15.066
There's very little food available;
we're just hoping to

00:13:15.066 --> 00:13:17.666
save it for the third day.
There's a chance on the third day.

00:13:17.666 --> 00:13:21.000
Going to solo Yanyue
O2 is a good option

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.666
since the altitude isn't
very high.

00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:25.466
If you feel unwell or are out
of breath going uphill,

00:13:25.466 --> 00:13:27.800
then you can still take
this supplement.

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:31.033
Take three pills,
and then you can take them once a day.

00:13:31.033 --> 00:13:33.433
I think one time is enough,
six hours is enough.

00:13:33.766 --> 00:13:39.566
As soon as you come out, you can see this gun
-wielding mountain.

00:13:39.566 --> 00:13:45.600
Inside, the weather around

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:51.600
Gun
-yama was very nice.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.200
It's very similar to the mountains
in Taiwan. We arrived at 5.9 meters,

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:59.333
which is actually quite close.
We found a helipad there.

00:13:59.333 --> 00:14:01.800
The space isn't very big,
but you really need to stop for a while.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:04.433
I sat on that chair XD I was trying
to sleep last night but didn't

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.166
sleep a wink and had to get up in
the middle of the night to watch.

00:14:07.166 --> 00:14:09.700
The stars are so beautiful,

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.533
they look like this, there are so many stars everywhere,
so actually the weather at night...

00:14:11.533 --> 00:14:13.566
Very good, it's usually a
summer afternoon thunderstorm.

00:14:13.566 --> 00:14:14.900
I actually sneaked into that

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.466
lounge room to say something.

00:14:16.466 --> 00:14:18.400
I wanted to sleep there, but I found out
that others were sleeping inside too.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.700
I thought to myself, "I can sleep now,
" but that person was also giving me...

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.000
Dog, dog, so I thought,
okay, forget it.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:26.400
I'll go back and lie down like this.
I need to prepare one.

00:14:26.866 --> 00:14:28.800
One small problem with these
powerful earbuds is...

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.466
I ate a lot and felt like my
stomach was full of poop,

00:14:30.466 --> 00:14:32.200
not knowing when it would explode,
but because of Japan...

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.300
Their habit is to urinate and
defecate in the mountain hut,

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:36.133
so they will definitely hold it in
until they reach the hut because...

00:14:36.133 --> 00:14:37.466
There must be toilets
in mountain huts,

00:14:37.466 --> 00:14:39.600
right? And there are many mountain huts along the way,
unlike in Taiwan, just like the one I saw today.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:41.600
If you want to liberate yourself
halfway through,

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.033
then you have to liberate yourself.

00:14:43.033 --> 00:14:43.833
Clamp and

00:14:43.833 --> 00:14:44.366
then down

00:14:44.366 --> 00:14:47.700
One reason why Taiwanese people like
to go mountain climbing in Japan is

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.700
that the mountain huts have been liberated
time and again is that...

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.566
Hiking in Taiwan is like being an ascetic;
I really don't want to.

00:14:53.566 --> 00:14:55.666
I think ordering food and bringing
it myself is perfectly fine.

00:14:55.966 --> 00:14:57.900
Of course, you can experience Japanese
culture in one or two meals.

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.900
I think it's okay to cook one or two meals myself.
What about yours?

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.500
For stoves (gas),
go to the local area like I did.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.266
You can buy 110 kcal of
gas at Good Day Villa.

00:15:04.266 --> 00:15:06.200
You can bring your own small
stove and cookware.

00:15:06.266 --> 00:15:08.033
I brought my own pot and cup,

00:15:08.033 --> 00:15:10.200
and I strongly recommend that even
if you're on a tour...

00:15:10.333 --> 00:15:13.033
Bringing a titanium cup would
also be great, I found.

00:15:13.033 --> 00:15:15.466
Many group members didn't bring their own cups,
so often...

00:15:15.466 --> 00:15:17.833
Do you want something to drink
or soak in a hot water?

00:15:17.833 --> 00:15:20.600
Tea is a bit of a hassle; it's
hard to borrow from them,

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.233
and there's nothing left to borrow.
They only have...

00:15:22.233 --> 00:15:23.800
Paper cups, and actually most of
the time you have paper cups.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:25.033
Consumption will lead

00:15:25.033 --> 00:15:25.866
to early use.

00:15:30.766 --> 00:15:31.766
You can bring your own tent

00:15:31.766 --> 00:15:35.700
to camp in the camping area.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.366
Yesterday, it was actually
quite cheap: 2000

00:15:38.366 --> 00:15:41.000
yen for foreigners and
1000 yen for students.

00:15:48.133 --> 00:15:52.800
This is where we can
cut it down tomorrow.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:58.233
The shortcut is to avoid
the Killing Hut.

00:16:00.366 --> 00:16:03.200
I haven't learned this Chinese character (how is it pronounced?).
Tomorrow I...

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.833
I might go to Yan Yue for a one
-on-one attack,

00:16:04.833 --> 00:16:06.833
and then I'll switch
back directly from here.

00:16:06.833 --> 00:16:07.833
Back at the gun hut,

00:16:18.066 --> 00:16:20.466
he used his iPad as a backpack.

00:16:20.466 --> 00:16:21.566
This board is awesome (using
an iPad as a back panel,

00:16:21.566 --> 00:16:23.733
lightweight?).

00:16:30.266 --> 00:16:34.266
I think there's a women's
mountaineering team ahead of us.

00:16:34.266 --> 00:16:37.700
The Japanese climb mountains
with great care (Poka: Yes,

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.300
they climb mountains with great care).
I think they are very...

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.633
When he shouts slogans in front,

00:16:42.633 --> 00:16:44.366
those behind him will
shout them back.

00:16:44.366 --> 00:16:48.266
Their shouts sounded like they were marching; they
had a marching style of mountain climbing.

00:16:48.266 --> 00:16:51.433
The captain and everyone's
pace was slow, but...

00:16:51.433 --> 00:16:54.066
They kept moving forward,

00:16:54.066 --> 00:16:57.333
all of them Japanese. Climbing mountains is a slow,
generally fast pace, and most of them are wearing...

00:16:57.333 --> 00:17:02.733
Heavy boots, and I noticed that La
Sportva appears frequently here.

00:17:02.733 --> 00:17:06.366
Very high and Salomon are the two most common
types of trail running shoes here.

00:17:06.366 --> 00:17:10.866
There are really very few trail running
shoes here due to cultural differences.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.366
He's very similar
to Nepal or South

00:17:15.366 --> 00:17:18.433
Lake; he's just very similar.

00:17:18.433 --> 00:17:21.733
A glacial landscape,

00:17:21.733 --> 00:17:27.400
then heading towards this plain,
ahead lies a very wide expanse.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:31.433
The valley is somewhat like South Lake;
heading towards the main peak,

00:17:31.433 --> 00:17:34.300
you should climb along
the green path.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.500
Go up there and you'll see
people turning around and going

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.900
up to the central peak,
2920, the last water source.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:44.800
I started imagining the route from
Taiwan to climb this mountain.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:50.600
Hello, keep trying your best!

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:53.400
Never mind, my Japanese
is just too bad.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:56.333
I really want to speak Thai.
Good luck with Thai...

00:17:56.333 --> 00:17:57.733
.......

00:17:58.066 --> 00:17:59.266
Fighting (??? No,

00:17:59.266 --> 00:18:01.233
this is Korean.
I've encountered them quite a lot too.)

00:18:01.233 --> 00:18:03.900
Koreans are foreigners,
but I think the majority are still...

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:06.766
Japanese people really do come
here to climb mountains.

00:18:06.766 --> 00:18:08.766
It wasn't just talk;
they really did come,

00:18:08.933 --> 00:18:11.133
and we ran into our women's
mountaineering team again.

00:18:11.133 --> 00:18:13.300
Very disciplined,
everyone marched in unison and

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.700
One sticks to the other,
and now we're going to keep going like this.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:19.100
If you take this route on
the scree slope in Taiwan

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.700
If Taiwan takes this route,
we will follow it.

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:26.533
If you don't know how to drive on this kind of road,
please use the gravel slope.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.033
The Japanese couldn't possibly
do something like this,

00:18:29.033 --> 00:18:33.066
with the upper central saddle point leading all
the way up from this side of the buttocks.

00:18:33.066 --> 00:18:34.100
Dangerous things happen
when Taiwanese

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:37.933
people are the audience.

00:18:37.933 --> 00:18:42.933
I don't know if it's the audience or not (awkward,
I admit it myself, haha). Go go go!

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:11.166
The annoying scree slope is just a matter of going uphill,
nothing to worry about.

00:19:11.166 --> 00:19:14.466
What's there to complain about?
I'm a little hungry.

00:19:14.933 --> 00:19:17.766
We should still bring
some rations because

00:19:17.766 --> 00:19:20.766
I just realized we finished
eating at 5 pm.

00:19:20.766 --> 00:19:24.766
There are actually seven hours
in between at midnight.

00:19:24.766 --> 00:19:27.766
One bread bar is OK
(the only one) for

00:19:30.933 --> 00:19:33.533
my teammate following behind me.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.000
Are you Taiwanese?! (You
just said it seemed

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:45.433
like we could take pictures?)
Sure, you can.

00:19:50.266 --> 00:19:51.733
(* &amp; ^% I joined a group tour...)

00:19:53.066 --> 00:19:54.600
(Laughed at XD) Remove the

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.100
water filter at 2500M.

00:20:08.766 --> 00:20:10.400
Strongly recommends bringing a 600
-1000ml

00:20:13.933 --> 00:20:14.833
water filter and some travel food.

00:20:14.833 --> 00:20:16.333
Do we have to wait

00:20:16.333 --> 00:20:17.866
or not? XD

00:20:17.866 --> 00:20:20.700
The two
-person team first went up to 2,

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:24.266
800, now it's 2,500.

00:20:24.266 --> 00:20:28.100
Climb 300 FLOW jelly,

00:20:29.266 --> 00:20:31.666
no water needed, just go to that...

00:20:31.666 --> 00:20:35.633
Cut down from the location of
Tenguhara to see the Emerald

00:20:38.466 --> 00:20:41.766
Pond and eat some red bean
sticks bought from Japan.

00:20:41.766 --> 00:20:43.700
(A little sweet)

00:20:45.433 --> 00:20:51.266
Bolong Cave

00:20:51.266 --> 00:20:54.200
He was accompanied by deities,
but he had a crack in his neck.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:04.200
I always thought there would be donkeys
coming down because of Nepal.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.466
Hearing the bell means
you're on the

00:21:05.466 --> 00:21:07.266
central sharp gravel
slope of the donkey.

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:20.466
The lightest fox
-themed long-sleeved shirt weighs only 100g and offers sun protection.

00:21:20.466 --> 00:21:24.200
Today I'm wearing a STATIC long
-sleeved t-shirt with fur trim.

00:21:27.733 --> 00:21:29.166
The two pockets

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:34.000
are very light

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.766
I guess the sweat will
come out of the jacket,

00:21:35.766 --> 00:21:36.800
so I'll try it later.

00:21:40.933 --> 00:21:43.300
A large patch of remaining
snow looks like

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:48.100
a scree slope on a snow
-covered mountain.

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:51.300
That section with the snowman
really looks similar,

00:21:51.300 --> 00:21:56.300
except this road isn't slippery and it's well
-paved, but it's still quite...

00:21:56.300 --> 00:22:01.466
Like the central tip Black
Diamond CARBON FKT

00:22:01.466 --> 00:22:04.999
Fasten it securely,

00:22:04.999 --> 00:22:08.300
it's very stable.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.666
This is the first time
I've used it for

00:22:09.666 --> 00:22:11.733
hiking; the last time
I used it in Thailand.

00:22:11.733 --> 00:22:15.933
It's great for trail running,
but has some minor drawbacks when climbing mountains.

00:22:15.933 --> 00:22:18.300
It's a trail running stick,
I think its height can't be adjusted.

00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:20.766
The uphill slope is a bit long,

00:22:20.766 --> 00:22:23.100
but you can change where you poke;
don't poke too high up.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:26.266
The person next to you should be positioned
lower to grab your height.

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:29.633
Normally, our height is 90
degrees above the ground,

00:22:29.633 --> 00:22:31.699
so you change the position
you're poking.

00:22:33.217 --> 00:22:35.933
I don't really use stacked stones or strips of cloth,
so I'll use this.

00:22:35.933 --> 00:22:37.233
The circle has moved
up to this position,

00:22:38.466 --> 00:22:43.800
the saddle of the spear.

00:22:43.800 --> 00:22:47.333
Flip over and you should
see the right

00:22:47.333 --> 00:22:49.733
side where the killing is located.

00:22:49.733 --> 00:22:54.033
The right cut at the saddle point is
the triangular point of the gun peak,

00:22:54.033 --> 00:22:57.800
with 900 meters remaining.

00:22:57.800 --> 00:23:01.733
Actually, this is because Gun
-dake

00:23:01.733 --> 00:23:02.766
is very close to the mountain hut.

00:23:21.366 --> 00:23:22.300
Arrived at the

00:23:23.425 --> 00:23:25.166
Killing Hut

00:23:28.666 --> 00:23:30.433
3 hours and 50 minutes,

00:23:30.433 --> 00:23:31.600
1100M 6KM

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:32.800
They're arriving

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:34.533
one after another!

00:23:34.533 --> 00:23:35.800
We couldn't resist and they
all ordered their meals.

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:39.666
Two hundred yen could be
exchanged for one liter.

00:23:39.666 --> 00:23:40.499
Eat some kappa gummies

00:23:47.866 --> 00:23:50.892
with hot water

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:54.966
Risotto (Italian
-style risotto) - Italian

00:23:54.966 --> 00:23:56.999
tomato risotto
- because of poor appetite.

00:23:58.866 --> 00:24:00.966
If you have a poor appetite,

00:24:00.966 --> 00:24:04.500
I suggest adding more water to this.

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:10.200
It tastes really good,
anyway it will turn into porridge or rice soup.

00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:11.666
It's quite exquisite,

00:24:11.666 --> 00:24:13.900
and it even has restaurant
-quality curry rice without meat.

00:24:13.900 --> 00:24:18.033
The curry rice (and it really

00:24:18.033 --> 00:24:20.133
didn't have any meat)~

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:25.037
Finally, more whey! (Did you

00:24:28.566 --> 00:24:30.633
come back from Gun
-gaku?)

00:24:30.633 --> 00:24:34.833
No (How could that be?) I've
already finished eating.

00:24:34.833 --> 00:24:36.600
You can buy wine for 3100.

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:41.266
It's very big and spacious.

00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:46.166
A private room is also
available for 16,

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:53.966
000 per night.

00:24:57.733 --> 00:25:01.900
This drying room looks like
this; it uses this huge

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:08.900
generator to produce large
quantities of...

00:25:08.900 --> 00:25:15.433
The water storage area is on Gun Mountain,
and you can still see people there.

00:25:16.833 --> 00:25:20.047
This area, up here, is called
Higashi Kamao Root.

00:25:20.099 --> 00:25:21.000
The road is actually the
same road that came

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:22.800
from Yan Yue and then
from Dong Jianwei.

00:25:22.800 --> 00:25:27.495
The area behind Shangqiangyue
is the proper one.

00:25:27.533 --> 00:25:28.500
Master Bolong (correction XD) first climbed
Gun Mountain in 1828 (37 years

00:25:28.500 --> 00:25:32.800
earlier than Edward Whymper's
first ascent of the Matterhorn).

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:36.233
I don't know if it's for commemoration,
so I put that...

00:25:36.233 --> 00:25:37.657
The location where it was named

00:25:58.233 --> 00:25:59.766
(Bolong Cave)
- Draft Beer

00:26:01.566 --> 00:26:03.833
Wine promoter (Thank you Poka,
tour leader, for the treat!!) Draft beer vinegar

00:26:08.566 --> 00:26:09.643
It has a mild,

00:26:10.300 --> 00:26:13.000
not overpowering,
alcoholic taste; it's drinkable.

00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:14.400
I really want to sleep right now,

00:26:14.400 --> 00:26:15.266
so I don't want to think
about anything else.

00:26:15.266 --> 00:26:19.966
Just a sip is enough,
everyone's chilling here now.

00:26:19.966 --> 00:26:22.200
The Japanese drink alcohol
while hiking,

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.733
but only if they can handle it.

00:26:23.733 --> 00:26:26.400
If you feel even slightly uncomfortable,
it's best not to eat too much.

00:26:30.133 --> 00:26:33.000
The Great Gun Mountain House returned
to the Killing Lodge.

00:26:33.000 --> 00:26:35.066
The forecast said it would rain
in the afternoon, so...

00:26:35.066 --> 00:26:37.966
This long
-lost rain skirt,

00:26:37.966 --> 00:26:41.900
along with warm trail running shoes near the thigh,
has reappeared.

00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:44.566
Rain will get your calves wet,

00:26:44.566 --> 00:26:48.066
but you need to control the temperature of your
thighs to maintain your core temperature.

00:26:48.066 --> 00:26:51.266
You can wear a rain skirt with GORE
-TEX shoes,

00:26:51.266 --> 00:26:55.400
or rain pants.

00:26:55.400 --> 00:26:57.366
Hiking in the wild is fine with a rain
skirt; it's even more convenient

00:26:57.366 --> 00:27:00.100
in Japan. We'll be going
into the drying room later.

00:27:00.100 --> 00:27:02.066
Just use this Keb

00:27:02.066 --> 00:27:03.966
little fox one.

00:27:03.966 --> 00:27:05.766
The GORE
-TEX three-layer raincoat has

00:27:05.766 --> 00:27:08.466
no weight limit for this trip (480g).

00:27:08.466 --> 00:27:13.400
This is perfectly fine
to use the little fox

00:27:13.400 --> 00:27:16.500
as an example; it's
completely harmless.

00:27:16.500 --> 00:27:19.966
Since it's a three
-layered raincoat, waterproofing shouldn't be a problem. Hopefully, it will be waterproof.

00:27:19.966 --> 00:27:25.200
I would prefer it to be on the
left or right or the side.

00:27:25.200 --> 00:27:27.266
There are two large pockets
on the chest area.

00:27:27.266 --> 00:27:30.100
It fits perfectly with a drawstring at the back of the hard
-top hat,

00:27:30.100 --> 00:27:34.333
and the Velcro strap on the wrist
is what I'm used to.

00:27:34.333 --> 00:27:36.700
The only minor drawback is
its relatively long shape,

00:27:36.700 --> 00:27:38.700
so size recommendations are needed.

00:27:38.700 --> 00:27:41.300
I tried it on; I wear size
M and it fits perfectly,

00:27:41.300 --> 00:27:44.000
not too tight.

00:27:44.533 --> 00:27:45.200
Wow, I've discovered a new

00:27:45.790 --> 00:27:47.790
world – breathable underarms!

00:27:48.466 --> 00:27:51.366
Just now, one of my teammates
said he would want

00:27:51.366 --> 00:27:52.900
to buy this,
so I immediately took it off.

00:27:52.900 --> 00:27:54.966
He tried it on and the
size was just right.

00:27:55.054 --> 00:27:57.900
This piece has a nice cut,
and I generally wouldn't choose green.

00:27:57.900 --> 00:28:00.966
This one is dark green, a very forest
-like dark green.

00:28:00.966 --> 00:28:03.300
Not the green uniform for soldiers (absolutely
not that kind of green!).

00:28:03.300 --> 00:28:05.633
I think it's great,

00:28:05.633 --> 00:28:07.266
the outfit change is complete.

00:28:07.266 --> 00:28:09.133
Switch to the Poratec beanie
vest OCTA. Like the Poratec,

00:28:10.266 --> 00:28:13.800
selecting the layer offers
two options: one is...

00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:15.666
Down filling plus a polar
alpha static base

00:28:15.666 --> 00:28:17.933
layer: 50% synthetic
fibers and 50% wool.

00:28:17.933 --> 00:28:20.000
I keep the short
-sleeved shirt as a spare; I wear

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:22.602
a 100% wool long
-sleeved shirt during the day.

00:28:22.633 --> 00:28:25.333
STATC pants (highly recommended!!)
are very lightweight.

00:28:25.333 --> 00:28:29.466
Even with STATIC trousers,

00:28:29.466 --> 00:28:32.533
my calves still get sore when going uphill,
so I still use COMPRESSPORT leg warmers.

00:28:32.533 --> 00:28:36.166
For very small pillows, I suggest you bring
your own (if you need a larger one).

00:28:36.916 --> 00:28:39.866
Wear it until bedtime,

00:28:39.866 --> 00:28:41.933
then take it off.
2RC + 1 protective capsule

00:28:41.933 --> 00:28:43.733
Take two more taurine tablets before

00:28:46.057 --> 00:28:48.199
meals to help you sleep.

00:28:48.199 --> 00:28:49.866
Dinner – This is what
we're eating

00:28:54.622 --> 00:28:57.666
at an altitude of 2877 meters!

00:29:02.066 --> 00:29:04.300
This is amazing! We've
been spoiled

00:29:04.300 --> 00:29:05.533
by the mountain huts in Japan!

00:29:05.533 --> 00:29:06.744
You have to pay your
debt tomorrow!! You

00:29:06.766 --> 00:29:08.600
have to pay your debt tomorrow (囧)

00:29:08.600 --> 00:29:10.733
Tomorrow this channel will officially
enter the main part,

00:29:10.733 --> 00:29:13.885
but we've already warmed up XD

00:29:14.354 --> 00:29:16.266
Montbell actually has this Nepalese
-style

00:29:16.692 --> 00:29:18.289
dressing table!

00:29:18.933 --> 00:29:22.914
Please be careful when you poop. If your phone falls into the latrine,
it means "NEVER PICK IT UP!"

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.433
Hi Poka, my diary has lost

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:55.366
a cute yet ugly kappa.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.933
The group members started eating energy
bars as soon as they set off, haha.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.566
(Seeing someone like Porter)
I'm gripping

00:29:21.828 --> 00:29:23.744
my hand really tightly right now!

00:19:48.933 --> 00:19:50.200
Do you lead tours?

